      "explanation": "Since \\(x\\%\\) means \\(x/100\\), taking \\(x\\%\\) of \\(x\\) means multiplying \\(x\\) by \\(x/100\\). Thus\n\\[\n\\frac{x}{100}\\cdot x=4,\n\\qquad\\text{so}\\qquad x^2=400.\n\\]\nThe two real numbers whose square is 400 are \\(20\\) and \\(-20\\). Because \\(x\\) is positive, \\(x=\\boxed{20}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
